      "side": 1,
      "message": "I really think one bit is enough.\nAdd macros : I2_CONFIG_MASTER defined a 0 to be consistent in the definition.",
      "revId": "ae98412d19524639dac96243d4f26f8175c95f66",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f6195673_6bbafc30",
        "filename": "include/i2c.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 28,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-03T17:48:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ll consider removing I2C_CONFIG_MASTER altogether, but I don\u0027t think defining I2C_CONFIG_MASTER to be 0 is a good idea. We should be able to check all I2C_CONFIG_* flags with \u0027\u0026\u0027, and I don\u0027t think it\u0027s a good idea to make I2C_CONFIG_MASTER special as it\u0027s likely to confuse programmers.",
      "parentUuid": "765c8636_26d21352",
      "revId": "ae98412d19524639dac96243d4f26f8175c95f66",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
