        "id": 1104704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-03T17:35:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you define 1 \u003d\u003d 10kpps for the speed, then we can fit all speeds in a uint8.",
      "revId": "ae98412d19524639dac96243d4f26f8175c95f66",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5625c29e_f6c955d2",
        "filename": "include/i2c.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-03T17:48:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it\u0027s going to confuse people, and I don\u0027t know how to name the field to make it non-confusing. \"myria\" is apparently the metric prefix for 10^4. I\u0027ll change it if you can think of a non-confusing name.",
      "parentUuid": "7643a650_3d59f23d",
      "revId": "ae98412d19524639dac96243d4f26f8175c95f66",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "96401a44_5a4ba25d",
        "filename": "include/i2c.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1104704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-11-03T18:01:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "According to Wikipedia \"(metric prefix): Not adopted by the International System of Units, therefore no longer used since 1960.\"\n\nuint8_t speed;                /* Speed in 10^4 bps */\nAnd then define \n#define I2C_SPEED_1000KHZ 100\n#define I2C_SPEED_400KHZ   40\n...\n#define I2C_SPEED_KPBS(speed) ((speed) * 10)\n\n\nOk, not great, but it still somewhat readable while preserving space.",
      "parentUuid": "5625c29e_f6c955d2",
      "revId": "ae98412d19524639dac96243d4f26f8175c95f66",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
